<Base title="Editorial policy — how BotPlanet researches and corrects" description="How BotPlanet researches, writes and corrects its content, including what happens when we get something wrong — published in the article, not a changelog.">
  <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="max-width:680px;">Independence and honesty come before commercial convenience.</p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The best-paying product is never made the best recommendation because of commission.</li>
    <li>Suppliers cannot edit an independent verdict; they may correct factual errors with evidence.</li>
    <li>Sponsored placements are clearly labelled and kept separate from rankings and reviews.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Evidence & claims</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Commercial and technical claims carry a source.</li>
    <li>Manufacturer claims we haven't independently verified are labelled as such.</li>
    <li>We show the evidence level for each product — from "researched" to "hands-on tested".</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Freshness</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices, stock and delivery show when they were last checked.</li>
    <li>Stale prices lose their "current price" label.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Spotted an error? Email us and we'll fix it and note the change.</p>
</Base>
